*>--- conformance-case
*> id: pb3829_rounded_bounded_function_modes
*> rules: [GR-14.7.4.3-1, GR-14.7.4.3-2, GR-14.7.4.3-3, GR-14.7.4.3-4,
*>    GR-14.7.4.3-5, GR-14.7.4.3-6, GR-14.7.4.3-7, GR-14.7.4.3-8,
*>    GR-14.7.4.3-9, GR-14.7.4.3-10, GR-14.9.8.4-2, GR-14.7.5-3,
*>    RV-15.8.4-1, RV-15.10.4-1, RV-15.11.4-1]
*> accept: [2014]
*> source-format: free
*> portable: unverified
*>---
*> kb/Work PB3829: a function whose returned-value rule bounds its value lands in the resultant identifier ROUNDED
*> by the statement's mode, exactly like any other arithmetic value. No rule bounds the STORED value.
*>  - 15.8.4 1) "The returned value is the approximation of the arccosine of argument-1 and is greater than or equal
*>    to zero and less than or equal to π."; 15.10.4 1) ASIN and 15.11.4 1) ATAN likewise bound the RETURNED value,
*>    which 15.4 places in "a temporary elementary data item".
*>  - 14.9.8.4 2) "The value obtained according to rule 1 is then stored, in conformance with the specifications in
*>    14.6.8, Alignment and transfer of data into data items, 14.7.4, ROUNDED phrase, and 14.7.5, SIZE ERROR phrase
*>    and size error condition". So the stored value is the returned value rounded per 14.7.4.3:
*>    rule 2 (no phrase = TRUNCATION), rule 3 AWAY-FROM-ZERO, rule 4 NEAREST-AWAY-FROM-ZERO (also the bare ROUNDED,
*>    11.9.6.3 2)), rule 5 NEAREST-EVEN, rule 6 NEAREST-TOWARD-ZERO, rule 8 TOWARD-GREATER, rule 9 TOWARD-LESSER,
*>    rule 10 TRUNCATION, rule 7 PROHIBITED (an inexact value is a size error and the receiver is unchanged).
*> The returned values, to more places than any leg needs: ACOS(-1) = 3.14159265..., ASIN(1) = 1.57079632...,
*> ASIN(-1) = -1.57079632..., ATAN(+-10^18) = +-1.57079632... (every implementation's approximation agrees to
*> far more places than the four the legs round at; none lies near a rounding boundary).
*> Three receivers: R4 (four places) where the NEAREST value lies ABOVE the bound in magnitude (3.1416 > pi,
*> 1.5708 > pi/2), R2 (two places) where it lies below (3.14, 1.57), and RP (PIC S9P, a trailing P, scale -1:
*> one unit is ten) where only the directed modes move the value off zero (AWAY-FROM-ZERO gives 10).
*> WHY EACH LEG CAN FAIL: a store that cuts the rounded value back inside the bound (the clamp PB3829 removed)
*> prints 3.1415 / 1.5707 on the R4 nearest legs and 00 on the RP AWAY-FROM-ZERO legs; a store that ignores the
*> mode prints the same value on every leg; a PROHIBITED store that does not see the inexact value takes NOT ON
*> SIZE ERROR and changes R4.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. PB3829ROUNDMODES.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 R4 PIC S9V9999 SIGN LEADING SEPARATE.
01 R2 PIC S9V99 SIGN LEADING SEPARATE.
01 RP PIC S9P SIGN LEADING SEPARATE.
